# Planned work

## Modular mpv scripts

- [ ] Use `--scripts=…` in mpv to declare the mpv-specific workflow modularly.

## Session/workspace workflow specification

- [ ] Define a session specification that gives one coaching session a stable
  name, workspace location, athlete/client context, source-media location, and
  destinations for analysis, annotations, exports, and backup.
- [ ] Add a shared `--session SESSION_NAME` option to workflow commands. It
  should select the session specification and provide default directories,
  rather than requiring each command to repeat a path.
- [ ] Decide how a session is created and stored (for example, a small
  file-based manifest under the workspace) and validate session names and
  paths before any file-moving operation.
- [ ] Make `msurf sd cp` / `msurf sd mv` resolve their destination from the
  selected session when no explicit `--dir` or `--subdir` is given.
- [ ] Extend the same session context to sorting, annotation, review, sync,
  report/export, and client-distribution commands where it is useful.
- [ ] Define precedence clearly: explicit command arguments override session
  values; session values override global config defaults; global config remains
  the fallback.
- [ ] Add dry-run output that shows the chosen session, resolved paths, and
  planned actions before a command copies, moves, or syncs media.
- [ ] Add fixtures/tests for session lookup, default resolution, invalid or
  missing sessions, and protection against paths outside the workspace root.
